  "articleBody": "When you're dreaming up your perfect tiny home, customizing the floor plan is where the magic really happens – but it helps to think through a few things first. You want your home to be a reflection of you, after all! First, really nail down your daily routines: do you cook a lot, work from home, or need space for a specific hobby? This helps determine zoning and feature placement. Next, consider who will be using the space regularly. Is it just you, a couple, or will guests be staying over? This impacts sleeping arrangements and common areas. Don't forget about your property itself – where will the home sit, what are the views, and how can you maximize natural light and outdoor connections? Zen Tiny Homes starts with a property assessment to weave these elements into your design. Finally, think about your budget and priorities. Customization offers incredible flexibility, but it’s essential to balance your wish list with practicalities. We specialize in developing custom floor plans that make the most of less space, ensuring your tiny home is not just a structure, but a truly high-functioning home designed around your daily life. Getting these considerations clear upfront makes the custom design process smoother and the end result much more satisfying. We're here to help guide you through every step.",
